# Go Rules

Use **@go** when working on Go codebases.

This rule references:

- **Go standards**: `@rules/go/standards.mdc` - the file unit, package design, errors, context, concurrency, testing, the gate
- **Go microservices** (services only): `@rules/go/microservices.mdc` - layering, resilience, observability

## Short summary

- A `.go` file holds one exported unit, named after it; this replaces the general one-declaration-per-file rule for Go.
- `codeality-go gate` is the definition of done. No `//nolint`.
- Keep handlers thin and domain logic isolated. See `@rules/core/boundaries.mdc` for the universal thin-handler principle.
